_pdbx_entry_details.entry_id                   1CHO 
_pdbx_entry_details.compound_details           
;1CHO
THE ALPHA CHYMOTRYPSIN MOLECULE IS COMPRISED OF THREE        1CHO
POLYPEPTIDE CHAINS WHICH ARE DERIVED FROM THE ZYMOGEN OF     1CHO
THIS ENZYME BY EXCISION OF RESIDUES 14-15 AND 147-148. TO    1CHO
ASSIGN SEPARATE CHAIN IDENTIFIERS TO THE THREE CHAINS        1CHO
WOULD OBSCURE THIS RELATIONSHIP AND SO THIS WAS NOT DONE.    1CHO
CHAIN TERMINATOR RECORDS WERE INSERTED AFTER RESIDUES 146    1CHO
AND 245 TO INDICATE EXPLICIT TERMINI AND THE SPECIAL CODE    1CHO
